==English==
{{wikipedia|Tweedledum and Tweedledee}}

===Etymology===
The names "Tweedledum" and "Tweedledee" first appeared in print in one of [[w:John Byrom|John Byrom]]'s epigrams, which satirised the disagreements between [[w:George Frideric Handel|Handel]] and [[w:Giovanni Battista Bononcini|Bononcini]]. They were made popular by [[w:Lewis Carroll|Lewis Carroll's]] ''[[w:Alice in Wonderland|Alice in Wonderland]]''.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# A fictional little fat [[man]] who is the twin brother of [[Tweedle-dum]] and appears in multiple artistic [[work]]s, including certain [[nursery rhyme]]s and Lewis Carroll's ''[[w:Through the Looking-Glass, and What Alice Found There|Through the Looking-Glass]]''.

